# Binary

<Aside title="Placeholder">

This page is a stub. Build instructions, a systemd unit example, and release-artifact references are still being written.

</Aside>

The server is a single compiled binary with no runtime interpreter. Deploying it is a matter of getting the binary onto the host, giving it the environment it needs, and supervising the process.

The shape of a binary deployment:

- Build with `cargo build --release -p wyrd-server`, or use a published release artifact once available.
- Provide the environment from [Configuration](/self-hosting/configuration/), including external Postgres, storage, and a signing key.
- Run it under a supervisor (systemd, or your platform's equivalent) that sends `SIGTERM` on stop so the server drains gracefully. Set the stop timeout above `WYRD_SHUTDOWN_DRAIN_MS`.

A systemd unit example and the release-artifact naming will land here.

